    "discuss the role the steamfitter plays in a safe work site.",
    "demonstrate all the major safety responsibilities of the steamfitter.",
    "identify types, sizes, and applications of steam piping.",
    "research proper practice for boiler safety and operation.",
    "apply the fundamental principles and uses of water/steam and other gases and chemicals in the piping industry.",
    "apply concepts in temperature, heat, and energy.",
    "utilize concepts in electricity including safety procedures, measurement, and simple calculations.",
    "describe the role of the apprenticeship as it relates to union employment.",
    "demonstrate proper use of basic drawing and measuring tools associated with the piping trade.",
    "interpret technical drawings and piping and plumbing diagrams in orthographic and isometric views.",
    "apply the uses and applications of Computer Aided Drafting (CAD).",
    "identify methods of joining pipes using compression and flanged joints.",
    "identify fittings, valves, clamps, and tools used in the industry.",
    "use an Oxy-Fuel torch to cut and weld materials properly and safely.",
    "use a shielded metal arc welder properly and safely.",
    "set up and calibrate orbital welders properly.",
    "describe and apply relevant plumbing codes and laws.",
    "use formulas to determine areas, angles, and volumes of pipes and vessels."
